{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Asks "},{"code":"authTokenInjector","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for a new token after a 401."}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Client"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refreshAuthToken","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"reason","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inRetryLoop","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The reason from the webhook response.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"reason"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether a retry loop got the 401.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"inRetryLoop"}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a loop, a failure is treated as transient: the previous token is kept and the loop is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still told to retry. Each failure in a row doubles the wait before the injector is called"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AuthRefreshBackoff\/delayMs(failures:)"},{"type":"text","text":"); a loop’s 401 that arrives sooner skips it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the loop’s retry waits until then, but at most 5s for it ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loopRetryDelay(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"). A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one-shot call ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inRetryLoop"},{"type":"text","text":" false) always calls it and gets its error thrown: the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retried on purpose, the token API may be back, and the injector’s error is how the app learns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"why it failed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each 401 makes its own call; they do not join one call, since an injector that never settles"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would then hold every later 401 too. A call that settles after a later one already set its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"token neither sets its own nor changes the backoff, so an older token never overrides a newer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and a call still pending when the client activates again does not override the new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session’s token. 401s that arrive together, such as the sync loop’s and the Watch streams’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the token expires, count as one failure."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The injector’s error, for a one-shot call.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Client\/refreshAuthToken(reason:inRetryLoop:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"Yorkie","externalID":"s:6Yorkie6ClientC16refreshAuthToken6reason11inRetryLoopySSSg_SbtYaKF","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refreshAuthToken"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reason"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"inRetryLoop"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}],"title":"refreshAuthToken(reason:inRetryLoop:)"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/yorkie\/client\/refreshauthtoken(reason:inretryloop:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","type":"topic","title":"Yorkie","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Client":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"code":"Client","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a normal client that can communicate with the server."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It has documents and sends changes of the documents in local"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the server to synchronize with other replicas in remote."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Client"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Client"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Client","type":"topic","title":"Client","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/client"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Client/refreshAuthToken(reason:inRetryLoop:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refreshAuthToken"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reason"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"inRetryLoop"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"title":"refreshAuthToken(reason:inRetryLoop:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Asks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authTokenInjector"},{"type":"text","text":" for a new token after a 401."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Client\/refreshAuthToken(reason:inRetryLoop:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/client\/refreshauthtoken(reason:inretryloop:)","role":"symbol"}}}